    {
      "en": " Zaid Ibn Arqam\nAnd Yaqubi writes in his Ta'rikh: \"A group of Muhajirs and Ansars kept themselves aloof from allegiance\nto Abu Bakr and had were followers of Hazrat ‘Ali.",
      "ur": null,
      "fa": null,
      "ar": null
    },
    {
      "en": " Among them were Abbas Ibn Abdu'l-Muttalib, Fazl\nIbn Abbas, Zubair Ibnu'l-'Awwam Ibn As, Khalid Ibn Sa'id, Miqdad Ibn ‘Umar, Salman al-Farsi, Abu\nDharr Ghifari, Ammar Yasin, Bara'a Ibn Azib, and Ubai Ibn Ka'b.\"",
      "ur": null,
      "fa": null,
      "ar": null
    },
    {
      "en": "\nWeren't these people the intellectuals of the umma?",
      "ur": null,
      "fa": null,
      "ar": null
    },
    {
      "en": " ‘Ali, Abbas, the uncle of the Holy Prophet and other\ndistinguished persons of the Bani Hashim - weren't these people wise and trustworthy?",
      "ur": null,
      "fa": null,
      "ar": null
    },
    {
      "en": " What kind of\nijma was it, which was held without the consultation of these people?",
      "ur": null,
      "fa": null,
      "ar": null
    },
    {
      "en": " When Abu Bakr is selected\nsecretly and other prominent companions are not informed, does this constitute ijma?",
      "ur": null,
      "fa": null,
      "ar": null
    },
    {
      "en": " Or is it political\nconspiracy?",
      "ur": null,
      "fa": null,
      "ar": null
    }
